# Build products: they are remade, and they weigh more than the source.
# The star is not tidiness. `target/` named one directory, and a second build
# directory called `target-int` once went in with an add of everything: 1.58 GB
# in 14,247 files. A name keeps out what it names; a shape keeps out what it is.
# But `cargo clean` empties `target/` and nothing else, so a sibling grows and
# is never reclaimed: a second build directory belongs INSIDE `target/`.
target*/
mutants.out/
mutants.out.old/

# The window: downloaded dependencies and the built bundle. The name stands
# without a path for the same reason as the star above: `desktop/node_modules/`
# kept out one directory, and a test runner's cache at the root went in.
node_modules/
desktop/dist/

# The native shell regenerates these on every build, from the icon and the
# configuration that are versioned. Android and iOS icons come from the same
# command: Sailor is a desktop program, and keeping them would version a
# hundred files for two platforms that do not exist.
desktop/src-tauri/gen/
desktop/src-tauri/icons/android/
desktop/src-tauri/icons/ios/

# The configuration of whoever works here, not of the product.
.claude/

.DS_Store
